{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRBvLV5NY9dUz8v2ZjdZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QEPfSHqSw8VYNM95BourLu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/impl388.md <<'EOF'\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/redact/rules.go` (new): add `var envNameRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*(_[A-Z0-9]+)+$`)` and `func envName(v []byte) bool { return len(v) <= 64 && envNameRE.Match(v) }`, with a comment: an all-upper-case snake-case value is an environment variable name, not a secret. It needs at least one underscore, allows no lower case, `+`, `/`, `=` or `.`, and is capped at 64 bytes. Also extend the comment above the `generic-assignment` rule to mention it.\n2. `internal/redact/scan.go`, `scanLine` (about line 104): make the skip apply to quoted and unquoted values, so `EnvAPIKey = \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"` and `token: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` are both covered: change `if placeholder(v) || entropy(v) < entropyThreshold` to `if placeholder(v) || envName(v) || entropy(v) < entropyThreshold`. Putting it here, not in `codeRef`, keeps `codeRef`'s unquoted-only contract. `placeholder()` would also work but is a less clear home.\n3. Corpus check (no code change expected): the specific-format rules in `rules.go` run on their own regexes and are unaffected (`AKIA…` has no underscore; `github_pat_`, `sk_live_` and `sk-ant-` contain lower case). Confirm that the `plantedTokens()` values in `internal/redact/helpers_test.go` are all caught after the change. The `generic-assignment` fixture is mixed-case random text, so it is still caught. Also run the `internal/redact` tests and grep the repo's other tests that use `Builtin()` for any all-caps underscore fixture. `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`-style names will now pass, and that is intended.\n4. `internal/redact/scan_test.go`: add tests (below). Build any credential-shaped fixture at run time (`\"api_\" + \"key\"`, `randStr`), or the diff guard will hold the worker's own change.\n5. `docs/proposal.md`: add one sentence in the secret-scan paragraph (the \"All agent output is committed too\" one, near \"Close-out then secret-scans the whole redacted log\"), saying that generic-assignment skips a value that is entirely upper-case snake case, as an environment variable name, and that the log scan, the committer scan and the diff guard share this rule. No new file.\n\n### Network inputs\nNone.\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `go test ./internal/redact/` (then `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...`).\n- New `TestScannerGenericAssignmentEnvNames` in `internal/redact/scan_test.go`, expecting zero findings, for:\n  - `EnvAPIKey = \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"`\n  - `token: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`\n  - `SECRET_NAME = \"GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY\"`\n  - `EnvOAuthToken = \"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"`\n  - a single-quoted form\n- Still-flagged cases in `TestScannerGenericAssignmentTruePositives`, or a sibling test:\n  - a lower-case value with underscores from `randStr` (for example `token = \"` + `strings.ToLower(randStr(21, 32))` + `_` + `...` + `\"`)\n  - a mixed-case value with underscores (`\"AbC_\" + randStr(22, 30)`)\n  - an upper-case value with no underscore (`strings.ToUpper(randStr(23, 32))`) is still flagged. It needs entropy of at least 3.5; if the seeded value scores lower, pick another seed.\n  - an upper-case value with `.`, `+`, `/` or `=` (for example `FOO_BAR+` + upper-case random text)\n  - an upper-case snake value over 64 bytes, such as 70 characters of upper-case random text split by `_`, is still flagged\n- Unit test for `envName` as a table: `A_B` true, `A` false, `_A_B` false, `A__B` false (the regex needs one or more characters after each underscore, so this is false), `A_b` false, a 64-byte value true, a 65-byte value false.\n- Existing tests, including `TestScannerPositivePerRule` and the log and committer tests, must pass unchanged.\n- Edge case: the capture class includes `.`, so `\"FOO_BAR_BAZ.\"` inside a sentence is captured with the dot, fails `envName`, and goes to entropy as today. That is acceptable and fail-closed.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. It loosens a security control that the log scan, the committer scan and the diff guard all share. The pattern is narrow (underscore required, no lower case, 64-byte cap), and the specific-format rules still run first. The residual risk is a real secret that is upper-case with underscores and sits next to a keyword. That is rare, because vendor keys mix case or use lower-case hex. No protected paths from `merge.protected_paths`, migrations or concurrency are touched; no public interface changes.\n\n### Size\nS (about 60 to 120 changed lines, mostly tests). Files: `internal/redact/rules.go`, `internal/redact/scan.go`, `internal/redact/scan_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`.\nEOF\nf=.ard/388/plan.md\nif [ -f $f ]; then echo exists; else printf '# Plan for #388\\n\\n' > $f; cat /tmp/impl388.md >> $f; fi\ncat > .ard/388/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a narrow skip so the generic-assignment secret rule ignores values that are entirely upper-case snake case, such as environment variable names. It is applied in the shared scanner, with table tests and a one-sentence doc note. Size S, risk medium because the log scan, committer scan and diff guard all share the rule.\n\n## Open issues\n- A reviewer should confirm the pattern stays narrow: an underscore is required, no lower case is allowed, and the cap is 64 bytes.\n- The worker must build credential-shaped test fixtures at run time, or the diff guard will hold its own change.\nEOF\ncat $f | head -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":21646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2137a05-9805-4c57-a7b8-f891cc8eee6a","uuid":"1c41ad39-b149-4f6f-89d8-7c5f3aa8ae8b","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:02:04.576Z","request_id":"req_011ChRBvLMNozVqE9AoiwxPx"}
